# Button haptics (`web-haptics`)

Commerce tap feedback is already wired. Do not add per-button `onClick` haptics.

- Package: `web-haptics`. Vendor adapter: `src/infrastructure/haptics/web-haptics/adapter.ts`
- Global listener: `HapticClickTracker` — wishlist / cart / checkout controls only (labels, `/cart` `/wishlist` hrefs, commerce analytics events)
- Android: `navigator.vibrate(30)` only while `userActivation.isActive`. iOS Safari has no Vibration API — plays a short click sound instead
- Unlock AudioContext on `pointerdown`; fire on `click`. Never call async `web-haptics.trigger()` on the audio path — Chrome then blocks vibrate and AudioContext
- Import `@/infrastructure/haptics` — never `web-haptics` from components. Opt out: `data-haptics-ignore`. Opt in: `data-haptics`

```tsx
// BAD — per-button SDK call
import { useWebHaptics } from 'web-haptics/react';
<button onClick={() => trigger('success')}>Add</button>

// GOOD — nothing extra; the global tracker handles the tap
<button type="button" aria-label="Add to cart">Add</button>

// GOOD — skip haptics for this control
<button type="button" data-haptics-ignore aria-label="Dismiss">×</button>
```
